<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of the Hevelli</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1150 CE (approx.) · capital Brandenburg an der Havel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Slavic principality on the Havel centred on Brandenburg, whose last prince bequeathed his land to Albert the Bear and so began the March of Brandenburg.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Hevelli, also called Stodorani, were West Slavic settlers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havel">Havel</a> lands west of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> from the 7th or 8th century. Their chief stronghold was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-an-der-havel">Brenna</a>, the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> an der Havel. In 928 to 929 the East Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> captured it in winter across the frozen marshes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Hevelli were governed by princes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-an-der-havel">Brenna</a>, controlling river crossings and fortified settlements on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havel">Havel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spree">Spree</a>. German rule after 929 was lost in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-slav-rising">Great Slav Rising</a> of 983, and the Hevelli joined, and later stood apart from, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lutician-federation">Lutician Federation</a>. The last prince, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pribislav-henry">Pribislav-Henry</a>, became a Christian and ruled as a German ally.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pribislav-henry">Pribislav-Henry</a> named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> his heir; on his death in 1150 Albert took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, securing it in 1157 after a fight with the Slavic prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaxa-of-kopenick">Jaxa of Köpenick</a>. The Hevelli lands became the core of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-brandenburg">Margraviate of Brandenburg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 800 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:75.62%;width:6.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brandenburg an der Havel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tugumir, Pribislav-Henry</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism, later Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polabian (West Slavic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hevelli, Stodorania</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=975&amp;focus=principality-of-the-hevelli" aria-label="Principality of the Hevelli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4962 369 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of the Hevelli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5282 625L5282 625"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5282 625h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5282 625h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5282 625h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Brandenburg an der Havel. <a href="/atlas?year=975&amp;focus=principality-of-the-hevelli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
